--TEST--
An attribute that is not `repeatable` is used once on one declaration, so a second use does not compile and is reported where it is written, with the first use named too — `rule:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-its-sites`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:attributes/an-attribute-is-declared-with-the-places-it-may-be-used
namespace Shop;

attribute Column on property { name: string }
repeatable attribute Tag on class { label: string }

abstract class Storable {
    attribute Table on class { name: string }
}

// `Tag` is `repeatable`, so this class may use it twice.
#[Tag(label: "catalog")]
#[Tag(label: "public")]
class Accepted {
    #[Column(name: "title")]
    public string $title = "";
}

class Refused {
    #[Column(name: "title")]
    #[Column(name: "heading")]
    public string $title = "";
}

// The short name and `Storable::Table` name the same declaration, so this is a second use too.
#[Table(name: "customers")]
#[Storable::Table(name: "clients")]
class Customer extends Storable {}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0763]: `Column` is used twice here, and its declaration is not `repeatable`
   --> case.nvs:22:7
%A
error[E0763]: `Table` is used twice here, and its declaration is not `repeatable`
   --> case.nvs:28:3
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
